null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nTested on Godot 4.4 beta 2 official\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.beta2 - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 2050 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6636) - 11th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-11400H @ 2.70GHz (12 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nIf you create an audio bus, and you add an PitchShift and an Reverb effect **in that order**. and you play the audio, all sorts of weird effects happen, and if you play the audio in the editor options, you may crash Godot.\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create an new project.\n2. Add an AudioStreamPlayer to scene tree, then add an audio file to it.\n3. Add an new audio bus, and add an PitchShift and an Reverb effect in that order to that bus.\n4. Make that audio stream player play on that bus\n5. Play the audio.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nProject: [audio-test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18626641/audio-test.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"IsaqueS","id":38296655,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4Mjk2NjU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38296655?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/IsaqueS","html_url":"https://github.com/IsaqueS","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IsaqueS/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IsaqueS/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IsaqueS/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IsaqueS/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IsaqueS/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IsaqueS/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IsaqueS/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IsaqueS/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.